## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/heatdistort.html
- Summary (EN): Heat Distort warps an input layer to imitate the shimmering haze seen around fire and mirage effects. It combines large-scale and fine-scale noise distortions to reproduce most common types of heat distortion.
- Résumé (FR) : Heat Distort déforme un calque pour imiter le miroitement de l'air chaud autour d'un feu ou d'un mirage, en combinant deux niveaux de bruit.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: original layer to distort", "effect: optional per-pixel scale for the distortion amount", "mask: optional per-pixel mask, scaled by the Mask parameter"]

- Key parameters: ["Distortion: overall strength, scaling both base and detail noise", "Element Size: pattern size in image coordinates; Per-Component Controls adds per-axis Element Scale", "Angle: direction of the distortion, where 0 points along positive X", "Accurate Distortion: traces curved paths for a more precise result, with a quality value", "Streak Blur: averages samples along the distortion direction", "Scale by Timestep: scales strength by the timestep, usually 1/FPS", "Base Distortion: large-scale waviness, with Distortion Scale and Element Size Scale", "Detail Distortion: finer distortion, with Cutoff and Roughness", "Blur Source: blurs the source in proportion to distortion strength, using Blur Scale", "Chromatic Aberration: per-channel offsets for colour fringing, with an overall Scale", "Animation: Time Offset, Pulse Length, Direction and Speed for drifting haze", "Mask: how much of the new value mixes with the original"]

- Caveats: ["With Accurate Distortion off, one step per pixel finds the source: fast but inaccurate when directions or scales vary", "With Accurate Distortion on, larger steps run faster but may miss intermediate variations", "Detail noise shows mainly where base distortion is strong; lower Cutoff to show it in weaker regions", "The page recommends Heat Distort By Layer for finer control of direction", "The noise algorithm and performance limits are not described"]

